They are blindly faithful devotees, but that is because Hindus understand very well that the cow is a mother. Childhood
In, we all have grown up with cow's milk, therefore cow is among our mothers. Undoubtedly, someone's
mother is sacred, therefore we should not kill a sacred cow. Pitrubhratru suhrjjantihinva sauratasauhridaah. The poor, the weak, and the needy are all in the midst of a great discussion. 37. Meaning of words.

Pitru—father; Bhratru—brothers; Suhrut— well-wishers; Gnati— relatives; Hitva— leaving;
Saurat— based on sexual relations; Sauhridah— the concept of friendship; Nanan— with relatives; Shyal— and relatives;
Samvadah— constantly in conversation; Dinah— miserly; Strinah— female devotee; Kalau— in the age of Kali; Naraah— man. In Kaliyuga, humans will be controlled by misers and women. They will abandon their father, brother, other
relatives and friends and associate with brothers-in-law and sisters-in-law. In this way, their
friendship will be based entirely on sexual relationships.
The Shudras will accept alms only from those who are sustained by the ascetic life. Having spoken of dharma, one should sit in the supreme posture of uttamasana. 38. Meaning of the word:

Shudra: - workers of the lower caste; Pratigrahishyanti: - will take religious donations; Tapah: - by pretending penance; Vesha: - and by dressing up as a saint; Upajeevinah: - while earning their livelihood; Dharmam: - regarding the principles of religion; Vakshyanti: - will speak;
Adharmaja: - unaware of religion; Adhirahuya: - climbing up; Uttam-asanam: - on a high seat. Cultured people will take donations in the name of God and, by pretending to be ascetics and by wearing the guise of monks, will run their livelihood. Those who do not know religion will sit on high seats
And will pretend to give discourses on religious principles. Meaning: Here, the inauspicious gurus, masters, priests, etc., are openly described. Always anxious, with a mind agitated, and full of worry. The fear of rain from the sky is dispelled. 39. Vaso, annapa, shayana, vyavasana, snana, abhushanaih.
Heena: The spectacles of demons will be seen by the people of Kali Yuga. 40. Meaning of words:

Nityam—Daily; Udvigna—Anguished; Manasah—Their minds; Durbhiksha—Famine; Kar—With tax; Karshitah—Weakened;
Niranne—When there is no food to eat; Bhu-tale—On the earth; Rajan—Oh King Parikshit; Aanavrishti—Drought; Bhaya—Fear;
Karan—Due to; Atura—Anguished; Vasah—Clothes; Anna—Food; Pana—Drink; Shayan—Rest; Vyayay—Sexual; Snan—Bathing;
Bhushanaih—With personal ornaments; Heena—Lacking; Pishacha-sandarsha—Like ghosts; Bhavishti—Will be;
Kalau—In Kali Yuga; Prajaah—People.
